<title>USA: Maxxim Medical stake cut by investor.</title>
<headline>Maxxim Medical stake cut by investor.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mississippi investor Donald DePriest said Thursday he has reduced his stake in Maxxim Medical Inc to the equivalent of 26,664 shares or 0.328 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, DePriest said he sold 435,000 shares in the Sugar Land, Texas maker of medical products between January 15 and April 10 at $13 to $14.69 each.</p>
</text>
